<% content_for :title, "About & FAQ · Gor's Coffee" %>
<main class="cafe-content-page" id="cafe-about" aria-labelledby="cafe-about-title">
  <header class="cafe-content-page__hero">
    <p class="cafe-content-page__eyebrow">Our story</p>
    <h1 id="cafe-about-title">A coffee experience, built for the web.</h1>
    <p>Gor's Coffee brings the café experience online. Explore the menu, customize a drink and build your basket.</p>
    <%= link_to 'Explore the menu', menu_path, class: 'cafe-content-page__button' %>
  </header>

  <section class="cafe-content-page__section" aria-labelledby="cafe-story-heading">
    <h2 id="cafe-story-heading">About this project</h2>
    <div class="cafe-content-page__grid">
      <article class="cafe-content-page__card">
        <h3>Browse</h3>
        <p>Search by product, explore categories and filter products using their dietary attributes.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="cafe-content-page__card">
        <h3>Customize</h3>
        <p>Choose available sizes and extras. A live estimate updates, while the server calculates the final basket price.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="cafe-content-page__card">
        <h3>Review</h3>
        <p>Update quantities and review a session-based basket. Orders are saved for testing only.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cafe-content-page__section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="cafe-faq-heading">
    <h2 id="cafe-faq-heading">Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <div class="cafe-content-page__faq">
      <details>
        <summary>Can I place a real order?</summary>
        <p>No. This is a portfolio demonstration. No physical café receives orders from this portfolio project.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Are these actual café prices?</summary>
        <p>No. Prices and products are illustrative.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How are prices calculated?</summary>
        <p>The browser displays an estimate while you choose options. The Rails server checks availability and saves its own calculation and configuration snapshot.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I use this site without an account?</summary>
        <p>Yes. You can explore the menu and try the basket in a guest session. The basket belongs to that browser session.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do you offer delivery or catering?</summary>
        <p>Not currently. The <%= link_to 'Catering concept', catering_path %> describes a potential website feature, not a live service.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cafe-content-page__section" id="location" aria-labelledby="cafe-location-heading">
    <h2 id="cafe-location-heading">Location & map</h2>
    <div class="cafe-content-page__location">
      <div class="cafe-content-page__map-placeholder" role="img" aria-label="Decorative conceptual street map; no real location or address is provided">
        <span class="cafe-content-page__map-mark" aria-hidden="true">GC</span>
        <span class="cafe-content-page__map-caption">Location not published</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>No physical café address</h3>
        <p>Gor's Coffee is a fictional digital storefront, so we do not display an invented map pin, address, opening hours or directions.</p>
        <p>If this template is adapted for a real café, a verified address and accessible map link can be added here.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cafe-content-page__section" id="contact" aria-labelledby="cafe-contact-heading">
    <h2 id="cafe-contact-heading">Contact & feedback</h2>
    <div class="cafe-content-page__card">
      <p>There is no customer service desk for this portfolio project. For technical project feedback, visit the public source repository.</p>
      <a class="cafe-content-page__button" href="https://github.com/TheGor-365/cafe_app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View the project on GitHub</a>
      <p class="cafe-content-page__fineprint">No real reservations, orders or support requests are handled here.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
